{"step_index":2754,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-27T13:06:08Z","input_tokens":2359,"cache_read_tokens":237023,"output_tokens":4959,"thinking":"Initial focus is on ensuring local storage correctly persists all relevant data after incorporating the new stylesheet modifications. The test suite aims to validate that problem status, notes, history, active stage, and learning settings survive modifications. This local persistence must function correctly without relying on any cloud-based backend.\n\n\nNow examining how to make the application data resilient to page refreshes and restarts by ensuring all relevant state (last opened problem, user code) is correctly saved and restored from local storage. The goal is to fully restore the application state after a new instance is created with the same local storage data.\n\nVerifying that the export function creates a valid JSON backup matching a defined schema, containing version, timestamp, stats, progress, roadmap, settings, and user code. The process also includes file naming and valid JSON string generation for downloads.\n\nNext, I need to comprehensively validate the import functionality. Robust error handling will reject malformed imports (empty, invalid JSON, non-objects, empty objects). Invalid problem IDs and stage numbers must be sanitized, and crucially, existing progress must be protected from corruption during invalid import attempts.\n\nFinally, comparing and contrasting import strategies: merge (combining progress data) and replace (overwriting data), noting which properties are preserved in each case. A prominent notice regarding local storage device portability will also be implemented.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"\"/**\\n * Comprehensive Test Suite for Phase 8: Local Progress Storage, Backup & Portability\\n * Validates zero-cloud persistence, page refresh restoration, export JSON,\\n * validation guard against malformed data, Merge vs. Replace strategies,\\n * preferences persistence, and engine integrity (Kadane = 6).\\n */\\n\\nconst fs = require('fs');\\nconst path = require('path');\\nconst vm = require('vm');\\nconst assert = require('assert');\\n\\nconsole.log('===================================================================');\\nconsole.log('PHASE 8 TEST SUITE: LOCAL PROGRESS STORAGE, BACKUP & PREFERENCES');\\nconsole.log('===================================================================');\\n\\nconst appBuildDir = 'C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/app_build';\\nconst problemsCode = fs.readFileSync(path.join(appBuildDir, 'dsa_problems.js'), 'utf8');\\nconst solutionsCode = fs.readFileSync(path.join(appBuildDir, 'dsa_solutions_data.js'), 'utf8');\\nconst dashboardCode = fs.readFileSync(path.join(appBuildDir, 'dsa_dashboard.js'), 'utf8');\\nconst engineCode = fs.readFileSync(path.join(appBuildDir, 'engine.js'), 'utf8');\\nconst stylesCss = fs.readFileSync(path.join(appBuildDir, 'styles.css'), 'utf8');\\n\\n// Mock browser DOM and environment\\nclass MockElement {\\n  constructor(tagName = 'div', id = '') {\\n    this.tagName = tagName.toUpperCase();\\n    this.id = id;\\n    this.className = '';\\n    this.classList = {\\n      classes: new Set(),\\n      add: (c) => this.classList.classes.add(c),\\n      remove: (c) => this.classList.classes.delete(c),\\n      contains: (c) => this.classList.classes.has(c),\\n      toggle: (c) => {\\n        if (this.classList.classes.has(c)) this.classList.classes.delete(c);\\n        else this.classList.classes.add(c);\\n      }\\n    };\\n    this.innerHTML = '';\\n    this.value = '';\\n    this.textContent = '';\\n    this.attributes = new Map();\\n    this.eventListeners = {};\\n    this.children = [];\\n  }\\n\\n  getAttribute(name) {\\n    return this.attributes.get(name) || null;\\n  }\\n\\\n<truncated 14072 bytes>","Description":"\"Test suite for Phase 8 Local Progress Storage\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/brain/4b927fe1-f9a3-4b3f-9f8a-92760e157eef/scratch/test_dsa_phase8_storage.js\"","toolAction":"\"Writing Phase 8 test suite\"","toolSummary":"\"Write Phase 8 test suite\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
